--
GCC alignment semantics in C++: aligned(n) increase-only on members and
class definitions, exact in a typedef, ignored on a class type in an
alias-declaration (g++); packed structs: byte-aligned members except those
with their own aligned(n); unnamed bit-fields occupy bits but never raise the
alignment; a two-attribute group on a member declarator keeps the base type
(`long m __attribute__((packed, aligned(2)))' had become an int).
